WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.040
Savage clone battles! Mind-bending time&nbsp;
travel! And more multiverses than you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.080
can possibly imagine! Keep watching for&nbsp;
more from the best sci-fi movies of 2022.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.600
From the creative minds that brought us Free&nbsp;
Guy, The Adam Project follows the titular Adam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.840
a time-traveling pilot from 2050 who becomes&nbsp;
stranded in 2022 while pursuing an unauthorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.880
mission. There, he meets his 12-year-old self,&nbsp;
and the two Adams must work together to accomplish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.720
older Adam's objective: Get back to 2018 to&nbsp;
save his wife's life. Same old same old, right?

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.187
"Unless it works like a multiverse, where each&nbsp;
ripple creates an alternate timeline. . ."

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:40.080
"It's not a multiverse! My God,&nbsp;
we watched too many movies."

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.000
But time travel has a way of making things&nbsp;
complicated - especially since older&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.320
Adam is fleeing a dystopian future.&nbsp;
With the odds stacked against them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.520
Big Adam and Little Adam decide&nbsp;
their only solution is to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.520
the man who actually created time travel&nbsp;
itself. . . their dearly departed dad.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.720
The Adam Project makes maximum use of Ryan&nbsp;
Reynolds' charisma, giving him a part that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.880
allows him to play excellently off his&nbsp;
younger self's vulnerabilities; notably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.640
newcomer Walker Scobell kills it here. Plus,&nbsp;
there are time jets. Who doesn't love time jets?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.280
After Yang is a deeply moving exploration of&nbsp;
memory and grief. In an idyllic-looking future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.440
parents Jake and Kyra have provided their adopted&nbsp;
daughter Mika with an android sibling named Yang.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.240
When Yang stops functioning, Jake promises Mika&nbsp;
he will have her "brother" back to normal as soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.760
as possible. But as they go through Yang's memory&nbsp;
bank, Jake and Kyra make several major discoveries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.120
about Yang's past and the true depths of his&nbsp;
soul. What emerges is breathtaking, emotional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.240
and profound - proving filmmaker Kogonada is&nbsp;
one of the very best directors working today.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.000
Writer-director Richard Linklater mixes&nbsp;
fact and fantasy in Apollo 10 1/2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.480
A Space Age Childhood. A kid&nbsp;
growing up in 1960s Houston,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.440
young Stanley is fired up by the Apollo&nbsp;
11 mission. As he watches history unfold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:04.080
the real details of the mission are interwoven&nbsp;
with his elaborate dream of being recruited as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.720
an astronaut - mostly because he's small enough&nbsp;
to fit in a lunar module's tight quarters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.920
Apollo 10 ½ embraces nostalgia without completely&nbsp;
ignoring the upheaval in America at this time:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.160
in this movie, Houston is just as fascinating a&nbsp;
setting as the moon. Meanwhile, rotoscoping - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.280
technology rarely used these days - captures&nbsp;
Stanley's imagination in suitably vivid fashion.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.160
In Belle, lonely teenager Suzu leads another&nbsp;
life in the virtual world known as "U." There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.320
she's a famous singer named Belle with&nbsp;
charming freckles and flowing pink hair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.400
After a concert is violently ruined by&nbsp;
a mysterious user known as the Dragon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.920
Belle sets out to find him. But she soon discovers&nbsp;
that they both have tragedy in their real lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.000
tragedy they must overcome together.&nbsp;
Belle features stunning visuals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.240
real emotional heft, rooted in all the&nbsp;
trials and tribulations of adolescence.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:00.160
Brian and Charles finds mild-mannered&nbsp;
Welsh inventor Brian creating a boxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.560
robot with a mannequin's head. After a&nbsp;
thunderstorm brings the automaton to life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.960
it dubs itself Charles and develops a keen&nbsp;
interest in everything the world has to offer.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.280
"Oh my gosh, what was that?"

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.522
"It's okay, it's okay."

00:03:12.522 --> 00:03:14.000
"Perilous, very perilous."

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.360
An unlikely friendship emerges as Charles grows&nbsp;
more and more human. At a brisk 90 minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.800
Brian and Charles offers the best&nbsp;
of intentions and a pleasantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.055
genial story that will no doubt&nbsp;
leave a smile on your face.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.760
Squishy body horror and nightmarish advanced&nbsp;
technology go hand in hand in director David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:37.120
Cronenberg's moody meditation on art and&nbsp;
humanity, Crimes of the Future. Cronenberg's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.640
sci-fi/horror hybrid revolves around&nbsp;
the evolution of the human body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.440
a government cover-up, and a&nbsp;
straight-up medical nightmare.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.880
Saul Tenser and his partner, Caprice, have&nbsp;
turned the surgical removal of his spontaneously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.840
growing new organs into performance art, which&nbsp;
attracts the attention of a group of radicals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.720
As you may have guessed,&nbsp;
this film is awash in gore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.320
Also notable is Kristen Stewart, who gives a&nbsp;
particularly nervy, off-balance performance as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:06.960
Timlin, an administrator at the National&nbsp;
Organ Registry. Stewart's weird energy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.040
a perfect tonic in Cronenberg's morbid&nbsp;
tale of surgery and sexual attraction.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.880
Sam Raimi infuses the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
with his trademark horror stylings in Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:22.320
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness. Superhero&nbsp;
sorcerer Stephen Strange must protect America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.960
Chavez, a dimension-hopping teenager,&nbsp;
from someone seeking to steal her powers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.360
Their flight across the multiverse takes them&nbsp;
to the very limits of existence, with Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.640
grappling with his own issues and confronting the&nbsp;
darkest and most disturbing versions of himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.040
Meanwhile, Wanda Maximoff emerges as the&nbsp;
emotional core of the film as she struggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.760
with the harrowing aftermath of WandaVision.&nbsp;
What results is a thrilling blend of terror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.640
fantasy, and sci-fi — one that proves the&nbsp;
MCU still has a lot of a heck to give.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.560
In the dystopian future of Dual, dying people can&nbsp;
arrange to have themselves replaced by clones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.600
But what happens to the clone if the original&nbsp;
person doesn't die? So begins Sarah's nightmare.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.680
After she survives a terminal illness,&nbsp;
Sarah's clone decides she wants to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:11.360
living Sarah's life. By law, only one Sarah can&nbsp;
remain alive, so the two must duel to the death.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.720
"We can't have two of you running&nbsp;
around forever. That'd be ridiculous."

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.720
In Dual, writer-director Riley Stearns&nbsp;
explores themes of identity in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.000
surprisingly comic fashion — despite the&nbsp;
devastating nature of this key dilemma.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.240
Simply put, Everything Everywhere All At&nbsp;
Once is one of the best films of the year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.200
An endlessly inventive and absurdist&nbsp;
delight, it stars Michelle Yeoh as Evelyn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.680
a middle-aged laundromat owner whose&nbsp;
IRS audit becomes a surreal adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:41.840
through the multiverse. As it turns out,&nbsp;
reality is threatened by a fearsome being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.040
and only Evelyn can rise up to be the savior&nbsp;
of every dimension. Multiple viewings are a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:52.320
must to catch every detail packed into this&nbsp;
wild, heartfelt, and colorful good time.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:57.120
King Car is a horror-comedy-sci-fi oddity&nbsp;
chock-full of political commentary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.840
The film stars Luciano Pedro Jr. as Un o,&nbsp;
a boy who can telepathically communicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.680
with cars. He refurbishes an old&nbsp;
automobile, the titular King Car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.320
providing it with the means to actually speak.&nbsp;
While Uno's power is exploited by his uncle Zé,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.800
King Car has its own ideas. The bizarro&nbsp;
absurdity of this one-of-a-kind film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.840
spins out of control at times, but King&nbsp;
Car is definitely a wild ride worth taking.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.080
At the beginning of Lightyear, audiences&nbsp;
are told upfront that this is the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.800
that made Toy Story's Andy&nbsp;
into a Buzz Lightyear fan.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.480
"To infinity. . ."

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.120
"And beyond."

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.760
The story sees the titular hero's headstrong&nbsp;
insistence on adventuring solo strand a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.000
ship full of his fellow Space Rangers on a&nbsp;
hostile planet. Buzz winds up working with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.680
this crew of lovable misfits, including&nbsp;
his former partner's granddaughter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.320
an adorable robotic cat named Sox, to make&nbsp;
things right. But can they overcome Zurg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.640
the enigmatic villain who is dead set&nbsp;
on sending waves of robots after them?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.360
Lightyear is a gorgeously animated sci-fi&nbsp;
adventure with plenty of comedy and heart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.200
It's at its best when spotlighting the crew's&nbsp;
attempts to figure out their strengths — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.840
when it indulges in its absolutely incredible&nbsp;
hyperspace sequences. Whether you're watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.280
it on an IMAX screen or Disney+, this Pixar&nbsp;
tale is sure to entertain and inspire.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:17.440
In Last Survivors, Troy and his son Jake live&nbsp;
in a remote haven, far from the horrors of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:22.240
post-apocalyptic landscape. Though Troy tells&nbsp;
Jake the world beyond is a nightmarish waste,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:27.120
that doesn't keep Jake from being fascinated by&nbsp;
Henrietta, a woman he meets while looking for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:32.640
medicine. Last Survivors distinguishes itself&nbsp;
from other post-apocalyptic films by focusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.800
on the characters' inner turmoil: here,&nbsp;
their emotional journeys take center stage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:41.520
rather than the ravages of World War III.&nbsp;
And the movie is made all the better for it.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:46.960
An adaptation of the celebrated German&nbsp;
film Run Lola Run, Looop Lapeta revolves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:52.480
around a fallen track star named Savi. With her&nbsp;
burgeoning athletic career derailed by injury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:57.360
Savi starts off in a dark place. Soon enough,&nbsp;
however, she falls in love with Satya,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.160
a charming criminal. After he leaves a bag of&nbsp;
cash on a bus, Savi must come up with the loot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.280
lest Satya be bumped off. But there's&nbsp;
a twist: Savi is stuck in a time loop.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.840
As the story replays over and over again, she&nbsp;
must use her knowledge to bring about better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:16.240
outcomes. More comedic than its source material,&nbsp;
Looop Lapeta is nevertheless a thrilling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.720
trip through alternate timelines, where the&nbsp;
slightest change can have massive repercussions.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.360
Neptune Frost is a singular work of Afrofuturism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:30.240
It's a sci-fi musical with an audacious&nbsp;
vision that mesmerizes even if, at times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:35.840
the story seems elusive. Set in Burundi, the&nbsp;
film follows a coltan miner named Matalusa and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:41.440
an intersex runaway named Neptune, whose coming&nbsp;
together gives birth to something incredible.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:46.720
At turns impressionistic and poetic, Neptune&nbsp;
Frost features characters with symbolic names&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:52.880
such as Memory and Psychology, and it primarily&nbsp;
concerns an anti-colonialist hacker collective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.480
waging technowar against an oppressive&nbsp;
police state. When Matalusa and Neptune meet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:02.080
it creates a jolt that powers the&nbsp;
collective's technological struggle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:08.320
Expect this movie's visuals and songs to get stuck&nbsp;
in your cerebral cortex for a long, long time.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.257
"What did you see?"

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:10.743
"Hmm?"

00:09:12.426 --> 00:09:13.420
"It was big."

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:14.912
"How big?"

00:09:14.912 --> 00:09:15.592
"Big."

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:21.680
Horror auteur Jordan Peele strikes gold yet&nbsp;
again with Nope, a sci-fi-horror film about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:27.200
siblings Emerald and OJ Haywood, horse wranglers&nbsp;
to the stars. When a UFO begins hovering above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:31.200
their ranch, they decide to catch it on tape&nbsp;
— but they're not the only ones with plans for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:36.400
the mysterious entity: Reporters, photographers,&nbsp;
and a sleazy former child star all have their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:42.480
designs. Nope tackles society's exploitation of&nbsp;
tragedy, humanity's relationship with animals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.960
and the treatment of below-the-line crew&nbsp;
on film sets. This makes for a layered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:51.280
experience that will have you questioning your&nbsp;
own assumptions from the very edge of your seat.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.960
Strawberry Mansion is a surreal sci-fi-rom-com&nbsp;
adventure starring Kentucker Audley as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.960
James Preble, a government agent who&nbsp;
audits people's dreams. That's right:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:06.240
In the future this movie imagines, dreams are&nbsp;
taxed. He soon discovers something more sinister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.520
afoot as he investigates Bella, an elderly&nbsp;
artist and the sole occupant of the titular home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:15.120
Full of bizarre logic, oddball&nbsp;
characters, and striking imagery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:20.412
Strawberry Mansion is a splendid head-trip&nbsp;
guaranteed to do a number on your imagination.

